id: pm-yrj7qr
title: "GH-942: expose the lightweight all-item metadata reader through the public SDK"
description: "GitHub issue https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/942 reports that listAllItemMetadataLight already powers the cheap CLI list path but is not exported through the public SDK, forcing package authors to choose heavier reads or private imports. Promote a typed, bounded public primitive with PmClient and narrow subpath parity."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-09T00:15:13.406Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-09T09:54:53.407Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-09T08:05:35.741Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-09T08:05:35.741Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "A documented public SDK primitive exposes the lightweight all-item metadata read without importing CLI or private core modules; top-level, narrow subpath, PmClient, and runtime action contracts have intentional parity; return types and omission semantics distinguish intentionally unavailable fields; import-cost, token, package-boundary, surface-snapshot, and complete coverage gates pass; a package-authoring example proves use from a compiled external consumer"
parent: pm-usfg
resolution: fixed
expected_result: Packages can use the lightweight all-item metadata reader through stable public SDK surfaces
actual_result: "Root SDK, sdk/runtime, and PmClient expose the host-aware lightweight reader with custom type-folder support"
